I think you need two things:

The survey design should be described more detail.  I had to guess that a "site" is a unique combination of Site and Trap.Number and that y1 is the observed status (0 or 1).  Also, it would appear that there is either a trap grid or collections of traps at specified distances from the road.  And there are "controls" which I can only assume aren't roads but yet there are the same set of distances associated with the controls.  You'll get much better advice here with a succinct set of details.

Your main question is about setting up the data with unmarkedFrameOccu.  That requires some rearrangement of your data.  Here's one way that doesn't require an additional package (such as the very nice arrayhelpers):
> > # Define function to rearrange data so that columns represent the size separate trap nights
> > rearrange <- function(id) {
> >   matrix(c(Odata[Odata$Trap.Night==1,id],
> >            Odata[Odata$Trap.Night==2,id],
> >            Odata[Odata$Trap.Night==3,id],
> >            Odata[Odata$Trap.Night==4,id],
> >            Odata[Odata$Trap.Night==5,id],
> >            Odata[Odata$Trap.Night==6,id]), ncol=6, byrow=FALSE)
> > }
> >
> > y <- rearrange(8)
> > obs.cond <- list(Trap.Status=rearrange(10), Species=rearrange(11),
> >   Sex=rearrange(12), Age=rearrange(13))
> > site.covs <- Odata[Odata$Trap.Night==1,c(1,2,3,9)]

> > umf<-unmarkedFrameOccu(y=y, siteCovs = site.covs, obsCovs = obs.cond)
> >

> > occu(~1 ~1, umf)
> > occu(~Distance.fromroad ~Treatment, umf)

