Dear unmarked users,

I want to calculate 95% CI for the parameter estimates in a distsamp model. The output when I call the model includes the z-score, p, estimate and standard error. Can I just use the standard error to obtain the intervals (Estimate ± SE x 1.96)? I realize this is a question related to statistics but I have only calculated CI in very basic scenarios (CI for means that I calculate). I just want to be completely sure that I am doing this correctly. Thank you very much in advance for any input and apologies for the very basic question.

Sincerely,

Lucas

