Thank you - has this update been included?
I was having trouble with using csvToUMF for a long format file with the regular installation: it was not recognizing my site variables. It seems like the most recent 'unmarked' version is from May 2017, so I suppose it has not been updated with this yet?
Everything worked great with Adam's github update (note for those on new Macs: you might run into issues with gfortran, see how to fix that here: https://thecoatlessprofessor.com/programming/rcpp-rcpparmadillo-and-os-x-mavericks--lgfortran-and--lquadmath-error/).

Also - note that the csvToUMF documentation says that the order of your data has to be id-observations-sitecovs-obscovs, which didn't work. When I put sitecovs at the end, it did work.

But overall, thanks so much for this update. This was driving me up the wall (my data set is so large, I couldn't figure out how to change it from long to wide myself either).

Geraldine

